+Adapted from P3-C11-DR01-D2A1-MUTATION-TRANCHE2-CONTINUE-02's tools/c5.py (blob 170e28aae923ea9af09b76e62d6ca45acecd28a2
+at b97205b2, the accepted dedicated C5 admission checker): the same parser and checks, for C24's one permitted warning
+group, C24's preserved Tranche-3 build, executable and worktree.
+
+The Sole Architect ruled C24's existing Tranche-3 mutant build ARCHITECT-ADMISSIBLE under a narrow C24-specific warning
+ruling (mission section 2). The ruling does not transfer (section 5): every other control's build keeps its own rule,
+and the general build classifier (classify.classify_build_success) is unchanged and still classifies the historical C24
+build `BUILD: NOT OK`. This module never rebuilds, never writes into the C24 worktree or its target, and never relabels
+the historical result.
+
+  admit(build_dir, ctl, synthetic=False)
+                            the dedicated C24 build-admission checker (section 8), over the preserved Tranche-3 build
+                            evidence (byte copies under inputs/c24/03-build, each authenticated against the Tranche-3
+                            packet's SHA256SUMS and git blobs). Admissible only if: the control is C24 (refused for any
+                            other control); A/B source EXACTLY_C_PLUS_PATCH before and after with the ruling's mutant blob
+                            and sha256; C the ruling's patch identity; D the exact build command and environment; E the
+                            exact toolchain and build inputs (those of the accepted C2 build and the accepted continuation
+                            builds; inputs C's blobs); F normal exit 0; G 16 GiB, zero swap, within 900 s; H no OOM, no
+                            signal; I no `error` diagnostic and no compiler-crash text; J exactly the one permitted warning
+                            group (header, primary location protocol.rs:739:5, every quoted source line equal to the
+                            mutant's, the caret run exactly under `Corrected` and the dash run exactly under `Resolve`,
+                            label and notes exactly the expected ones); K every other stderr line is cargo progress, the
+                            group's own lines, cargo's summary of exactly one warning, the Finished line or the
+                            Executable line (no other warning, lint or diagnostic); L cargo named exactly one
+                            library-test executable; M its recorded sha256 and size equal the ruling's; and the
+                            historical classification is BUILD: NOT OK with exactly one failed check, the general
+                            classifier's `no error or warning diagnostic`. synthetic=True is for t3_controls.py's tampered
+                            copies only: the preserved-receipt identity check is replaced by a failing line, so a
+                            synthetic copy is never admissible, and every other check runs.
+  pin(ctl, build_dir)       the preserved executable pin (section 9): a regular file, not a symlink, every path component
+                            real, beneath the C24 worktree's own real target directory (not a symlink, not a mount point);
+                            executable bit; sha256 and size exact; dep-info identity as recorded, naming the executable and
+                            the worktree's protocol.rs; release/deps holding exactly the two recorded nexus_governed_control
+                            artifacts; no file or directory under the target modified (mtime or ctime) after the build
+                            record finished.
